> complex (1+2i)/(3-i)
(1+2i)/(3-i) = 1/10 + 7i/10
  Re = 1/10,  Im = 7/10
  check: equal numerically (0.1 + 0.7i, complex arithmetic)
> polar x + i y
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
x + i y = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*e^(i*atan2(y, x))
  = sqrt(x^2 + y^2)*(cos(atan2(y, x)) + i*sin(atan2(y, x)))
  r = |z| = sqrt(x^2 + y^2),  theta = arg z = atan2(y, x)
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi; undefined where x = y = 0
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-16)
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-16)
> trig sin(x) cos(x)
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of sin(x) cos(x)
  product to sum: sin a cos b = (sin(a + b) + sin(a - b))/2, cos a cos b = (cos(a - b) + cos(a + b))/2, sin a sin b = (cos(a - b) - cos(a + b))/2
    = sin(2x)/2
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 6e-17)
  exponential (Euler): sin u = (e^(iu) - e^(-iu))/(2i), cos u = (e^(iu) + e^(-iu))/2
    = (exp(i*x) - exp(-i*x))*(exp(i*x) + exp(-i*x))/(4*i)
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
  simplest: sin(2x)/2  (product to sum)
